{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg decoding pipeline jpeg decoding pipeline","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","fileName":"JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Decoding Pipeline","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[JPEG Compression Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg decoding pipeline jpeg decoding pipeline","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","fileName":"JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Decoding Pipeline","heading":"JPEG Decoding Pipeline","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The JPEG decoding pipeline reverses the lossless coding steps, restores quantized frequency coefficients, applies the inverse discrete cosine transform to each block, and converts luminance and chrominance data back into displayed color pixels.\n\nIt cannot undo the rounding performed during encoding. Missing coefficients are estimated only through the stored quantized values, which is why successive saves can accumulate distortion and why prior quantization may remain detectable after a second compression.","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Decoding Pipeline.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"